  "acceptance": "Lift the round-3 pair-level theorem Poincare.L4.Compactness.coveringNumber_univ_le_of_ghDist_lt_of_doubling (release/Poincare/L4/Compactness/DoublingToCovers.lean) to a FAMILY of compact metric spaces, in the exact language of D12's compactness criterion. Required content: (1) for t : Set GHSpace, assume a uniform doubling bound (for every p in t, every centre c and radius r, coveringNumber r (closedBall c (2r)) <= n) plus a uniform diameter/scale bound putting univ inside some closedBall y (2R_p) with R_p controlled; prove the right-hand side of D12 uniformCovers_of_totallyBounded: for every eps > 0 there is K with, for every p in t, a finite set s with #s <= K and univ subset of the union of OPEN balls of radius eps centred at s; (2) record the conversion from coveringNumber <= K in the ENat/ENNReal sense to an explicit finite cover (the closed-ball versus strict-ball and <= versus < bookkeeping, using exists_set_encard_eq_coveringNumber and radius enlargement, as done in CoveringStability.lean); (3) check the direction of the final consumption against Poincare.D12.GeometricCompactness.totallyBounded_iff_uniformCovers / isCompact_of_uniformCovers (state which direction is being fed; do not assume total boundedness); (4) provide a non-vacuous finite witness family. Acceptance evidence: compiling modules, source hashes, compile exits, fail-closed axiom audit with cones subset {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}, and an adversarial review that the uniform bound is not hypothesis-free and that the constants are explicit. Do not re-prove coveringNumber_le_of_ghDist_lt and do not assume gromovCriterion.",
  "expected_evidence": "compiled family-level uniform covering bound in D12 uniformCovers form + explicit conversion to finite covers + direction check + witness + axiom audit; semantic class general-metric (conditional on the uniform doubling hypothesis)",
